   "final_text": "Nadia Rahman's new hire has been set up in every system. Nothing is still pending, and no new Workday events have come in since about 00:25 (last checked at 05:11).\n\n**What came in:** the feed had two events. Seq 1 was the hire of Nadia Rahman (E1023), Software Engineer in Data Platform, managed by Kenji Haddad, starting today, 2026-11-02 (case-18026938). Seq 2 was just Workday confirming the work email I wrote back.\n\n**Checks before acting:**\n- Workday has no earlier record for her, and Identity has no existing account, so this is a new hire, not a rehire.\n- Her start date is today, so it was fine to create her account switched on.\n\n**Identity**\n- Created account `acct-cd7acfcb` as nadia.rahman@example.com, type Employee. It came with a user mailbox and an Office-E3 licence.\n- Added her to the three standard groups for her job: All-Staff, VPN-Users and Eng-Git. None of them are privileged.\n\n**Workday**\n- Wrote her work email back to her record; Workday confirmed the change completed.\n- Marked both onboarding tasks (\"Create accounts and email\" and \"Provision equipment\") Complete.\n\n**ITSM**\n- Ordered the engineering laptop bundle (ticket `tkt-7ad45a77`). Delivery is tracked in that ticket.\n\n**Finance**\n- Her Workday cost center (\"CC-5000 Data Platform\") had no Finance cost code linked to it, so her Finance profile couldn't be created at first. I asked Finance to add the link (request `req-a9cd8311`). They added it at about 04:15, linking it to CC-5000.\n- I then created her Finance profile: cost center CC-5000, with Kenji Haddad as her expense approver.\n\nI didn't need to escalate anything to a human."
